    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "How do you know when summer is near? Is it the sweet smell of gardenias"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "栀子花"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Or maybe the buzzing of cicadas"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "蝉"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Did you know there’s a science to understanding the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "timing",
            "ref": "v-timing"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of these seasonal events and their changes? It’s called phenology."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Phenology is a key part of life on Earth. Many birds time their nesting. They make sure that their eggs hatch"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "孵化"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when insects are plentiful so that they can feed their babies. Many farmers and gardeners use phenology, often without even realising it. For example, they plant carrots and cabbage when the first lilac"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "丁香花"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " leaves appear."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Phenology affects many "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "aspects",
            "ref": "v-aspect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of nature, including the water and carbon cycles. These cycles play a key role in regulating the Earth’s climate. But due to climate change, many phenological events are now changing. Spring events are occurring earlier than in the past, and fall events are happening later. This is true all over the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scientists aren’t sure what these changes mean for biological"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "生物学的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " systems. Many problems could "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "arise",
            "ref": "v-arise"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One of them is called phenological mismatch. This happens when animals and plants respond differently to climate change. Species that depend on each other can suffer terribly. For example, if a plant flowers before the pollinators"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "授粉生物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " arrive, both the plant and the pollinators might "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "struggle",
            "ref": "v-struggle"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to survive."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If you’re interested in these cycles of cause and effect, you can take a closer look at some phenological events. Record the weather daily, and note the dates when different plants bud"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "发芽"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and flower. After several years, you’ll notice that these events don’t occur on the same date every year. At the very least, you’ll get a better understanding of how climate change is affecting the world around us."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
